            <ArticleTitle>Aspergillus Mycetoma Causing Epiphora and Ipsilateral Facial Pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S25-S27</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/IOP.0000000000000681</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tearing is a frequently encountered chief complaint in an ophthalmologist's office. Certain associated atypical symptoms may warrant further workup. The authors present a case of a patient presenting with painful tearing which elicited further evaluation with CT imaging. This revealed a maxillary sinus fungus ball as the cause for the patient's tearing.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
